    {
      "id": 22,
      "name": "Triple Triad explainer",
      "x": 13,
      "y": 2,
      "width": 32,
      "height": 32,
      "visible": true,
      "type": "npc_spawn",
      "npcId": "triple_triad_explainer",
      "sprite": "guide",
      "dialog": [
        "I'm here to explain the rules of Triple Triad.",
        "Which topic do you want to learn about?",
        "Triple Triad is a game played with special cards",
        "placed on a 3x3 board.",
        "Each card has 4 numbers on it, one per side.",
        "These numbers are so-called stats.",
        "Players take turns placing cards on the board. As",
        "they do so, they try to capture and gain control of",
        "their opponent's cards.",
        "That's where the numbers come in. If a player",
        "places a card with a higher number next to a card",
        "with a lower number, the player captures that card.",
        "Thus, the goal of the game is to gain control of more",
        "cards than the other player by the end of the game.",
        "There are a number of optional game rules you can",
        "apply to individual games.",
        "They can affect card stats, how cards capture",
        "each other, the scoring and the prizes.",
        "When you win a game, you will recive 1 random",
        "card from your opponent from their Deck.",
        "This also works the other way around: if you lose,",
        "you have to give your opponent one of your cards,",
        "chosen at random.",
        "You can change what you win or lose from a game",
        "by using an optional game rule."
      ],
      "team": [],
      "trainer": false
    },
